#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c0b4ea8-c305-52fb-b738-39b52cd65224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\notin N,$ or $x$ is not positive." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401751} {:answer/id #uuid "0f89fefa-c3c4-5941-854f-f243eb5a7db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\in N,$ and $x$ is positive." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401752} {:answer/id #uuid "fa092300-5642-58f4-a90f-6ea2281b0263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\in N,$ or $x$ is positive." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401753} {:answer/id #uuid "064a345b-f5c1-5e19-82b0-253407d0787b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\notin N,$ and $x$ is positive." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401754} {:answer/id #uuid "54036453-852b-5e55-ab90-eafbae198c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\notin N,$ or $x$ is positive." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54036453-852b-5e55-ab90-eafbae198c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\notin N,$ or $x$ is positive." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401755} :answer-field/id #uuid "75c6802b-9187-56f8-8a12-dde53fdaa099" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2d8f44ce-e231-5920-980e-3c7663e37fa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-183349" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $x\\in N,$ then  $x$ is positive.\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x\\in N.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is positive.\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x\\notin N.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\notin N,$ or $x$ is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80e50955-37f8-51bc-83cc-cb950145c252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472820} {:answer/id #uuid "495a8b40-49df-5a56-9235-6ebb943146aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "495a8b40-49df-5a56-9235-6ebb943146aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472821} :answer-field/id #uuid "33d25ffd-2c6e-5b5b-99df-560a24530be3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1322f1f2-f4c5-54d8-87cc-355df640d02d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472822} {:answer/id #uuid "33f4cad9-66cd-545d-9ac0-97d5414f12cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33f4cad9-66cd-545d-9ac0-97d5414f12cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472823} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aeb8409-1020-570b-8cec-0822b2e40889" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ff70513-8053-559e-b6b1-7a97e4aa128d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472824} {:answer/id #uuid "78ab4291-cd70-5529-b069-e726e0430998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ff70513-8053-559e-b6b1-7a97e4aa128d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472824} :answer-field/id #uuid "aebe7e6e-372c-5557-a0e2-e163a4bed7dd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d6a13d3-ad69-5578-b6a3-a3b3842749f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-183354" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\ge 2.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $-x\\le -2.$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n- **I.** If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ and if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n- **II.** $x\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $-x\\le -2.$\n- **III.** If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ or if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\ge 2$ if and only if $-x\\le -2.$\n\n- $x\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $-x\\le -2.$\n\n- If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ and if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407603 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198260 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c5f2a86-209a-5bb3-a3f2-77d679adb0a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5893e887-eb3b-5990-8e74-a074a1a5182c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10,20,25,30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407581} {:answer/id #uuid "6c0f2522-98d4-5781-bab7-2ccffef0e1af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5,10,15,30,35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407582} {:answer/id #uuid "7fde4c43-2c7b-5b42-a18e-e6d5c2b96d2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407587} {:answer/id #uuid "cc049350-ae56-5686-858f-6f49ce3f97bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10,20,30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407595} {:answer/id #uuid "e83ceacd-7bdb-5677-92b5-c8f925ae70c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5893e887-eb3b-5990-8e74-a074a1a5182c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10,20,25,30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407581} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c48ea9-d964-59bd-a88d-64bcb5ade0c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ea344c4-f70e-5016-bcc7-6af9f4085a8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-183376" :question/problem "For the universal set $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU={5,10,15,20,25,30,35},\n$$\n\nfind the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ for the following predicates: \n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is odd.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $\\sqrt{x}$ is integer." :question/worked-solution "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={5,15,25,35}\n$$\n\nand its complement is\n\n$$\n{\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}={10,20,30}.\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}={25}\n$$\n\n \nand its complement is\n\n$$\n{\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}={5,10,15,20,30,35}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & ={5,15,25,35}\\cap {25} \\\\  & ={25} \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & ={10,20,30}\\cap {5,10,15,20,30,35} \\\\  & ={10,20,30} \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & ={25}\\cup {10,20,30} \\\\  & ={10,20,25,30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
